Task 3: Using Map (Hardcoded Data)
Objective: Store hardcoded data in a Map and send it to the JSP.
URL: http://localhost:8080/product
Map Data:
Product ID : 1001
Product Name : Laptop
Brand : Dell
Price : 65000

Use:
Map<String,Object> map=new HashMap<>();
map.put("id",1001);
map.put("name","Laptop");
map.put("brand","Dell");
map.put("price",65000);
model.addAllAttributes(map);
JSP Output:
Product Details
Product ID : 1001
Product Name : Laptop
Brand : Dell
Price : 65000
Display using:
${id}
${name}
${brand}
${price}
No JSTL.
What You Will Learn
Creating multiple controller methods.
Passing hardcoded data using Model.
Using model.addAttribute().
Creating and using Map<String,Object>.
Passing all map values using model.addAllAttributes().
Displaying data using JSP EL (${...}).
MVC Flow: Browser fi Controller fi Model/Map fi JSP fi Browser